{"page_content": "5.1\nExperiment Requirements\nFLEX-2\nSRD Rev. 1\n5.1.2\nDroplet Deployment and Ignition\nDroplet sizes, during FLEX-2 experiments, will vary between 1.5 mm and 5.0 mm. A measured\nquantity of fuel is dispensed from a fuel reservoir and deposited onto the support \ufb01ber using\na suitable deployment technique (e.g., opposed-needle technique used in DCE or single-needle\ntechnique implemented in the ground-based rigs). A subset of tests will require that the droplets\nare deployed on support \ufb01bers equipped with either a single pinning bead (i.e., for the slow\nconvective \ufb02ow tests, as discussed in Section 2.5) or a set of pinning beads spaced a distance,\nL , apart (i.e., droplet array tests, as discussed in Section 2.6). In addition to the subset of\ntests requiring a beaded \ufb01ber it will also be required to provide the option for all tests, at\nthe discretion of the researcher, of deploying droplets onto a beaded or an un-beaded \ufb01ber.\nThis option would be exercised when the the researcher feels it is warranted either to ensure a\nsuccessful droplet deployment or to take advantage of \ufb01ber pyrometry.\nFollowing droplet deployment, after a preset dwell time designed to allow droplet surface oscil-\nlations to die out, the fuel vapor/oxidizer mixture is ignited using a minimum ignition energy.\nPrevious experimental results show that deployment-induced droplet surface oscillations die out\nwithin a second. The ignition system should be capable of waiting for a predetermined dura-\ntion for these oscillations to die out. Immediately following ignition, the ignitor, as well as all\nother hardware should be removed from the test region. This zone-of-exclusion is de\ufb01ned as a\nspherical region extending at least 10 initial droplet diameters in the radial direction from the\ndroplet center.\nDroplet size:\nDroplet diameters shall vary from 1.5 mm to 5 mm \u00b1 0.25 mm.\nDroplet reproducibility:\nDroplet size shall be reproducible to within \u00b1 5%.\nDroplet support \ufb01ber:\nA support \ufb01ber (i.e., either a wire or \ufb01ber), used to anchor the\nposition of the droplet within the camera\u2019s FOV, shall have a diameter less than 100 \u00b5m.\nThe material used for the \ufb01ber shall have incandescent properties comparable to that\npossessed by an 80 \u00b5m SiC \ufb01ber, such that the emission intensity can be calibrated against\na blackbody source to allow for indirect temperature measurement using thin \ufb01lament\npyrometry techniques with the existing HiBM\u2019s camera and LCTF con\ufb01guration. It is", "metadata": {"source": "FLEX-2 SRD Final.pdf", "page": 40}}